= The old address keeps the sign

PiS still owns offices, loyal councils and the name that won 2015. It no longer
owns the queue. Candidates, donors and broadcasters who once waited for a
place on its lists now ask Mentzen and Bosak first.

The change reaches people before it reaches statute books. A hospital director
delays guidance because a future minister has promised reversal. A registry
calls equal marriage a disputed procedure. Police describe intimidation
outside both buildings as a public-order disagreement. No national repeal has
passed; institutions are already rehearsing one.

KO and PSL spokespeople reject the word "cordon" and ask instead which wing of
Konfederacja can sign a stable agreement. PiS has become another bidder for
the same coalition.

- @freebie_crossover_services
